      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That hollow ache is the hardest kind of silence—it doesn't ask for patience, it asks for surrender. Maybe the well isn't dry; maybe you've just been drawing from the wrong one, and the real water is deeper than you've ever dared to reach. You don't have to find the spark again; you just have to let the shell crack open and see what's actually inside. And if that feels impossible, then let the motions be enough for now—they're still keeping you alive until the real you is ready to return.",
